@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1791 = private unnamed_addr constant [1086 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `pytest.raises` calls without a `match` parameter.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`pytest.raises(Error)` will catch any `Error` and may catch errors that are\0Aunrelated to the code under test. To avoid this, `pytest.raises` should be\0Acalled with a `match` parameter. The exception names that require a `match`\0Aparameter can be configured via the\0A[`lint.flake8-pytest-style.raises-require-match-for`] and\0A[`lint.flake8-pytest-style.raises-extend-require-match-for`] settings.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\0A        ...\0A\0A    # empty string is also an error\0A    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\22\22):\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport pytest\0A\0A\0Adef test_foo():\0A    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\22expected message\22):\0A        ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.raises-require-match-for`\0A- `lint.flake8-pytest-style.raises-extend-require-match-for`\0A\0A## References\0A- [`pytest` documentation: `pytest.raises`](https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/reference.html#pytest-raises)\0A", align 1
