@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1855 = private unnamed_addr constant [542 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `and` expressions that contain falsey values.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf the expression is used as a condition, it can be replaced in-full with\0A`False`.\0A\0AIn other cases, the expression can be short-circuited to the first falsey\0Avalue.\0A\0ABy using `False` (or the first falsey value), the code is more concise\0Aand easier to understand, since it no longer contains redundant conditions.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aif x and [] and y:\0A    pass\0A\0Aa = x and [] and y\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aif False:\0A    pass\0A\0Aa = x and []\0A```\0A", align 1
