@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1888 = private unnamed_addr constant [760 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports that are not at the top of the file.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAccording to [PEP 8], \22imports are always put at the top of the file, just after any\0Amodule comments and docstrings, and before module globals and constants.\22\0A\0AThis rule makes an exception for both `sys.path` modifications (allowing for\0A`sys.path.insert`, `sys.path.append`, etc.) and `os.environ` modifications\0Abetween imports.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A\22One string\22\0A\22Two string\22\0Aa = 1\0Aimport os\0Afrom sys import x\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport os\0Afrom sys import x\0A\0A\22One string\22\0A\22Two string\22\0Aa = 1\0A```\0A\0A## Notebook behavior\0AFor Jupyter notebooks, this rule checks for imports that are not at the top of a *cell*.\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#imports\0A", align 1
