@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1974 = private unnamed_addr constant [2647 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unused imports.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUnused imports add a performance overhead at runtime, and risk creating\0Aimport cycles. They also increase the cognitive load of reading the code.\0A\0AIf an import statement is used to check for the availability or existence\0Aof a module, consider using `importlib.util.find_spec` instead.\0A\0AIf an import statement is used to re-export a symbol as part of a module's\0Apublic interface, consider using a \22redundant\22 import alias, which\0Ainstructs Ruff (and other tools) to respect the re-export, and avoid\0Amarking it as unused, as in:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom module import member as member\0A```\0A\0AAlternatively, you can use `__all__` to declare a symbol as part of the module's\0Ainterface, as in:\0A\0A```python\0A# __init__.py\0Aimport some_module\0A\0A__all__ = [\22some_module\22]\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0A\0AFixes to remove unused imports are safe, except in `__init__.py` files.\0A\0AApplying fixes to `__init__.py` files is currently in preview. The fix offered depends on the\0Atype of the unused import. Ruff will suggest a safe fix to export first-party imports with\0Aeither a redundant alias or, if already present in the file, an `__all__` entry. If multiple\0A`__all__` declarations are present, Ruff will not offer a fix. Ruff will suggest an unsafe fix\0Ato remove third-party and standard library imports -- the fix is unsafe because the module's\0Ainterface changes.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport numpy as np  # unused import\0A\0A\0Adef area(radius):\0A    return 3.14 * radius**2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef area(radius):\0A    return 3.14 * radius**2\0A```\0A\0ATo check the availability of a module, use `importlib.util.find_spec`:\0A\0A```python\0Afrom importlib.util import find_spec\0A\0Aif find_spec(\22numpy\22) is not None:\0A    print(\22numpy is installed\22)\0Aelse:\0A    print(\22numpy is not installed\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Preview\0AWhen [preview](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/preview/) is enabled,\0Athe criterion for determining whether an import is first-party\0Ais stricter, which could affect the suggested fix. See [this FAQ section](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/faq/#how-does-ruff-determine-which-of-my-imports-are-first-party-third-party-etc) for more details.\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.ignore-init-module-imports`\0A- `lint.pyflakes.allowed-unused-imports`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `import`](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-import-statement)\0A- [Python documentation: `importlib.util.find_spec`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/importlib.html#importlib.util.find_spec)\0A- [Typing documentation: interface conventions](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/source/libraries.html#library-interface-public-and-private-symbols)\0A", align 1
